  "decision_conditions": [
    "The development to which this permission relates must be begun not later than the expiration of three years beginning with the date of the decision notice. \r\rReason: To comply with the provisions of S.51 of the Planning & Compulsory Purchase Act 2004.\r",
    "The development hereby permitted shall be carried out in accordance with the following approved plans:\r\rE 00\rE 01\rE 02\rE 03\rE 04\rE 05\rP 01\rP 02\rP 03\rP 04\rP 05\rP 06\rP 07\rSuDs Proforma\rHighway Safety Impact Form\r\rReason: For the avoidance of doubt and in the interests of proper planning.\r",
    "The use of the property as a House in Multiple Occupation hereby approved shall be occupied by a maximum of 6 people at any one time and shall not be subdivided or occupied as self-contained units. \r\rReason: To accord with the stipulations of definition as a House of Multiple Occupation and to safeguard the residential character of the surrounding area.\r",
    "No independent cooking or laundry facilities shall be installed in any of the respective bedrooms, and the communal kitchen / dining room shall be retained in perpetuity.\r\rReason: To accord with the stipulations of definition as a House of Multiple Occupation and to safeguard the amenity of neighbours and the residential character of the surrounding area.\r",
    "The development shall be carried out in accordance with the approved refuse storage details as set out in drawings P 01 and P 07 before the development is occupied. The refuse storage shall be retained and maintained as such for the lifetime of the development.\r\rReason: To ensure the provision of refuse storage in accordance with the London Borough of Enfield - Waste and Recycling Planning Storage Guidance 2024\r",
    "Notwithstanding the approved plans, prior to first occupation, cycle parking shall be provided in compliance with the following criteria:\r\rProvision of a minimum of six long stay cycle parking spaces in the front garden area\rin an accessible location, should be step free and involve no more than 2 doors or gates (excluding the store door)\rsecured: with a British Standard mortice lock or access fob\rfully enclosed: 4 walls and a roof\r\rReason: The Council's Climate Action and Transport Policies seek to increase the use of active and sustainable transport modes. This means that access to bicycle parking should be easy and secure to remove potential barriers to cycling.\r"
  ],
